{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTubeReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTubeReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.TypeTags.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.D_charm7_crossing_collides_etaPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.D_charm7_crossing_collides_etaPhi","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L189-L201","doc":"**A hypothetical charm `= 7` would collide too** — kept as a\nrobustness remark, NOT as a corpus fact.\n\nThis previously read \"under the other corpus value charm `= 7`\n(`knot-notation-convention` row 9)\". **There is no such corpus\nvalue** (correction at Obstruction B above): the corpus fixes charm\nat `n = 5`, and `7₁` on the adjacent line is the tau lepton. The\narithmetic below is true and worth keeping — it shows the\ndegeneracy is not an artifact of the particular assignment, since\neven a counterfactual `n = 7` would land on `η/φ`'s crossing count\n— but it must not be cited as evidence of corpus ambiguity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.winding_content_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.winding_content_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L151-L187","doc":"**The winding dictionary is not injective.** It cannot separate\nthe D meson from the kaon, though they are physically distinct\n(`m_D ≈ 3.8·m_K`). Hence the gg→`c̄c` operator-selection input for\nthe D meson is *not* canonically fixed by the `T(2,n)` winding\nnumber alone: a weak-isospin (up/down-type) grading orthogonal to\n`n` is the missing datum.\n\n**REFINED 2026-08-24.** Non-injectivity is a property of\n`windingContent`, which maps each meson to a `Multiset ℕ`. The\ncorpus itself *does* separate charm from strange: table 2 gives\n`c = T(2,5)` and `s = T(2,5)^σ`, and `σ` is present iff the quark\nis down-type across all five quark rows (`u/d` at 3, `c/s` at 5,\n`b` at 7). `knot-notation-convention.md` defines\n`T_{m,n}^σ = T_{m,-n}`. So the degeneracy is this projection\n**discarding `σ`**, not an absent structure — the discriminator\nsurvives one level up.\n\n**WEAKENED on a second pass, same day.** The caveat above read\n\"`σ` is overloaded … whether it *is* `T₃` is the open question\".\nThat is too generous. `knot-notation-convention.md` *documents*\n`σ` on a knot as **charge conjugation** (\"the superscript\ndistinguishes a particle from its antiparticle via mirror\nreflection\"), instantiated on leptons as electron `T(2,3)` /\npositron `T(2,3)^σ`. Under that meaning the quark rows assert\n`d = ū`, `s = c̄`, `b = t̄` — charge `−1/3` identified with\ncharge `−2/3`, which cannot be intended.\n\nSo `σ` cannot be the `T₃` grading *as documented*: one superscript\ncarries two relations and only the unusable one is defined. The\n5/5 down-type alignment is real and suggestive, but the\ndiscriminating assignment is **undefined**, not merely\nunprojected — a prerequisite for the `T₃` work rather than a step\nwithin it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.D_kaon_same_winding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.D_kaon_same_winding","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L144-L149","doc":"**D and kaon carry the same winding content.** With charm `= 5`\nthe open-charm D meson `{c̄=5, u=3}` and the kaon `{ū=3, s=5}` are\nthe *same* multiset — so every symmetric function of the windings\n(crossing count `n₁+n₂ = 8`, product, …) agrees on them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.windingContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.windingContent","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L133-L142","doc":"The **generation-winding content** the `T(2,n)` dictionary sees:\nthe unordered pair `{n₁, n₂}` of the two quark windings, with the\ncorpus assignment `u,d = 3`, `s = 5`, and **charm `= 5`**\n(`knot-formula-table` row 11). The operator-selection / crossing-\ncount rule is a symmetric function of this multiset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.instDecidableEqMeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.instDecidableEqMeson","kind":"instance","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.Dmeson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.Dmeson","kind":"ctor","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.etaPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.etaPhi","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.kaon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.kaon","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.pion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson.pion","kind":"ctor","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.Meson","kind":"inductive","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L124-L131","doc":"The four meson generations of `lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary`,\nplus the D meson. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_winding_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_winding_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L114-L120","doc":"**The winding number is a complete invariant of a 2-strand\nbraid.** `B₂ → ℤ` is a bijection: the whole carrier is fixed by\none integer, which cannot index a hyperbolic knot family (the\n`T(2,k)` closures are `Vol = 0` for every `k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_commutator_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_commutator_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**The commutator is trivial on `B₂`.** `⁅a,b⁆ = 1` for all\n2-strand braids — the sharp contrast with `B₃`, whose nontrivial\ncommutator subgroup houses the Brunnian/hyperbolic Borromean. A\ncarrier with trivial commutator admits no Brunnian linking, hence\nno hyperbolic bound-state volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.twoStrand_comm","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**2-strand braiding is commutative.** `B₂` is abelian — the meson\ncarrier retains no braiding degree of freedom beyond its winding.\nContrast `B₃`, which is nonabelian: exactly the room the\nhyperbolic Borromean `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.TwoStrandWinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.MesonFluxTube.TwoStrandWinding","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/MesonFluxTubeReduction.lean#L91-L96","doc":"The **winding group of a 2-strand braid**, `B₂ ≅ ℤ`. With fewer\nthan three strands the braid relation cannot be written, so `B₂`\nis the free group on the single generator `σ₁`, i.e. `ℤ` (written\nmultiplicatively). This is the object the naive single-tube\nreduction lands in. ","signatureChunk":0}]}